 \paragraph{External validity.}
-The timing measurements use two one-stage detectors (YOLOv8n, YOLOv5s); for three newer YOLO models (YOLOv8s, YOLO11n/s, YOLOv12n) only candidate counts from historical data are available, without latency. One dataset family (COCO), 100 measured images and five patch seeds. NMS-free detectors, quantized models and accelerators are not covered. The whole-image attacks are adaptive variants from public code, not reproductions of the original experiments, and require white-box access; patches are inserted digitally, without print-and-capture tests. The case-study optimizer is gray box and does not minimize latency directly; the paper claims neither an attack stronger than previous work nor a denial of service on any deployed system.
