 \paragraph{Conclusion validity.}
-Effects are read against the MDE; a confidence interval containing one, or an effect below the MDE, is reported as not detected at that sensitivity, not as equivalence. The analyses are estimates with confidence intervals, not a family of tests, so no multiple-testing correction is applied. The threshold $N^{*}$ is read on a sparse grid and is sensitive to noise near the threshold.
